Oxidation state of iron $\left(x^{2}\right)$ in $\mathrm{K}_{4}\left[\mathrm{Fe}(\mathrm{CN})_{6}\right]$ is

\begin{array}{r}
4+x+6 x(-1)=0 \\
x=2
\end{array}

In $\left[\mathrm{CoF}_{6}\right]^{3-}, \mathrm{F}^{-}$is a weak ligand. It cannot pair up $d$-electrons and form outer orbital octahedral complex while $\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ and $\mathrm{CN}^{-}$are strong ligand.

In $\left[\mathrm{CoF}_{6}\right]^{3-}$, outer orbital $4 d$ is used in hybridisation. Thus, it is called outer orbital or high spin or spin free complex.

\mathrm{Co}=[\mathrm{Ar}] 3 d^{7} 4 s^{2} \text { and } \mathrm{Co}^{3+}=[\mathrm{Ar}] 3 d^{6}
